WEBVTT

00:08.700 --> 00:12.160
Since it's already arrived 
at the disposal site,

00:12.160 --> 00:13.880
it's not possible to recover it.

00:13.880 --> 00:15.240
That's what they told me.

00:16.060 --> 00:19.640
I heard that industrial waste 
behind the main building...

00:19.640 --> 00:23.060
was scheduled to be disposed of this weekend....

00:23.630 --> 00:30.520
No one informed me or any of the teachers
 that the schedule had been changed.

00:48.750 --> 00:53.000
If I'd looked into things more thoroughly, 
then this wouldn't have happened.

00:54.060 --> 00:55.770
I can't apologize enough.

00:57.810 --> 01:00.160
I see.

01:01.060 --> 01:03.960
No, if it was a paperwork error, then...

01:03.960 --> 01:05.570
There's nothing we could have done.

01:05.570 --> 01:07.440
What will we do now?

01:07.440 --> 01:09.580
I have no choice.

01:11.340 --> 01:13.840
Since it's come to this...

01:12.440 --> 01:13.840
...come to this!

01:13.840 --> 01:17.470
With the power of my Black Card!

01:17.470 --> 01:21.180
With my savings!

01:21.180 --> 01:22.340
I said no!

01:21.180 --> 01:22.340
You can't do that!

01:22.850 --> 01:25.280
That's where we have to draw the line.

01:25.280 --> 01:27.250
Yasaku-san is right.

01:27.670 --> 01:30.320
Then what are we gonna do?

01:30.320 --> 01:33.950
All the notable shipping companies 
and factories, plus Waku Wan...

01:33.950 --> 01:37.910
We already asked for all their pallets and 
other materials they didn't need, meow...

01:57.330 --> 01:58.630
I guess we head home?

03:29.520 --> 03:33.940
<b>Step 10
"DIY" Means... Rock Bottom? Impossible?
With Courage and Drive, Anything is Possible!</b>

03:49.670 --> 03:51.370
Um, Miku-san...

03:51.760 --> 03:52.940
Bless you.

03:53.500 --> 03:56.020
You didn't have your raincoat?

03:58.110 --> 04:01.130
I just forgot to put it on, that's all.

04:01.350 --> 04:03.180
<i>She's that depressed?</i>

04:03.960 --> 04:05.200
Serufu, too?

04:06.420 --> 04:08.550
She was in a daze.

04:11.300 --> 04:14.060
Well, that's understandable.

04:14.060 --> 04:18.140
To think that all the materials 
you managed to gather are gone...

04:20.260 --> 04:22.170
Let's get you a warm bath.

04:23.060 --> 04:25.900
Indeed! Leave it to me!

04:27.980 --> 04:29.200
I'm gonna sleep.

04:29.720 --> 04:30.550
What?

04:30.690 --> 04:31.520
What?

05:06.690 --> 05:07.800
There it is!

05:08.820 --> 05:11.330
<b>Serufu • Miku</b>

05:13.330 --> 05:15.320
Coming!

05:16.950 --> 05:20.350
Oh, Purin-chan! Welcome.

05:20.710 --> 05:21.840
Hello.

05:23.200 --> 05:26.450
May I... impose on your 
hospitality for a little while?

05:31.830 --> 05:33.230
Of course!

05:33.740 --> 05:35.540
Serufu is in her room.

05:39.470 --> 05:41.280
Serufu, are you there?

05:41.810 --> 05:42.860
I'm coming in.

05:53.760 --> 05:55.240
I'll be imposing on you for a little while,

05:55.240 --> 05:57.320
Pochi, Tama, Meat.

06:02.240 --> 06:03.260
Serufu.

06:10.870 --> 06:12.800
I heard from Jobko-chan.

06:13.210 --> 06:14.570
About the tree house...

06:15.250 --> 06:17.870
She said materials you'd gathered 
for the secret hideout...

06:17.870 --> 06:20.090
were all gone.

06:24.110 --> 06:27.610
And so... I was just thinking...

06:27.610 --> 06:31.050
This time, instead of places like 
factories and businesses...

06:31.550 --> 06:36.300
maybe you could try gathering 
materials from regular homes.

06:37.370 --> 06:40.460
I think that every house 
has broken chairs...

06:41.060 --> 06:43.740
or other things like desks they don't need.

06:44.930 --> 06:46.680
Something like an old cutting board...

06:47.110 --> 06:48.410
Could you use that?

06:49.420 --> 06:51.820
The school bulletin board...

06:52.370 --> 06:54.570
and... Is it called Waku Waku Wan Wan?

06:55.180 --> 06:58.030
You could try asking the store 
to post fliers for you.

06:59.350 --> 07:01.730
It's stuff that no one needs anyway, right?

07:01.730 --> 07:03.810
I'm sure they'd be happy to give it to you!

07:04.440 --> 07:08.120
DIY is supposed to use those 
kind of things anyway, right?

07:08.600 --> 07:11.110
Not that I really know anything about it.

07:11.730 --> 07:14.580
"Even dust becomes a mountain when 
it's piled high enough," right?

07:15.960 --> 07:18.200
Here. I'll give this to you.

07:18.470 --> 07:20.370
So, you know...

07:20.770 --> 07:22.540
Cheer up!

07:22.540 --> 07:24.510
Say, "I guess it's okay,"

07:24.510 --> 07:27.610
and, like you always do, 
keep looking ahead...

07:27.610 --> 07:28.500
Okay?

07:34.550 --> 07:38.060
<b>Serufu • Miku</b>

07:43.940 --> 07:45.840
This brings back memories!

07:45.840 --> 07:48.560
Oh. Huh? Purin?

07:48.560 --> 07:49.700
Huh?

07:51.850 --> 07:53.760
Why are you here?

07:53.760 --> 07:54.920
What?!

07:58.460 --> 08:03.020
I-I heard that all the materials for 
the secret hideout were gone,

08:03.020 --> 08:06.050
and I thought you might be depressed, 
so I came because I was worried!

08:06.470 --> 08:09.170
For materials, if you used places 
like the school bulletin board

08:09.170 --> 08:11.310
and asked every household 
for things they don't need,

08:11.310 --> 08:13.440
then you could probably gather quite a lot!

08:13.710 --> 08:15.630
Here! Some materials!

08:15.630 --> 08:18.360
The remnants of the bench that was 
in the garden a long time ago!

08:24.530 --> 08:26.230
You're amazing, Purin!

08:26.420 --> 08:27.280
What?

08:27.760 --> 08:30.950
You were thinking exactly the same thing!

08:31.400 --> 08:32.530
What?!

08:33.350 --> 08:37.690
When we asked people for lumber they didn't 
need, broken desks, things like that...

08:37.690 --> 08:40.340
we gathered up a <i>huge</i> amount of stuff!

08:40.740 --> 08:42.500
"Gathered"?

08:42.500 --> 08:44.010
That's right!

08:52.120 --> 08:57.450
We could have made a thousand secret hideouts 
and then we got overrun with members...

08:57.830 --> 09:00.400
Serufu, you...

09:01.080 --> 09:05.110
You were in a daze the whole time... 
That's what Jobko-chan told me.

09:06.620 --> 09:08.910
But you were just having fun 
imagining what to do, weren't you?

09:08.910 --> 09:09.720
Huh?

09:10.240 --> 09:11.190
What's this?

09:11.190 --> 09:12.640
Is this my room?

09:13.080 --> 09:15.350
So, I came home without even realizing it?

09:16.730 --> 09:18.560
When did I change my clothes?

09:25.540 --> 09:28.040
<b>Serufu • Miku</b>

09:28.800 --> 09:31.560
I really loved this.

09:34.050 --> 09:40.240
Purin, your dad got some of the bowling 
alley's floor and brought it back, right?

09:40.240 --> 09:41.880
Did he?

09:41.880 --> 09:44.050
Oh, yes, you might be right.

09:45.530 --> 09:46.570
Yeah.

09:46.570 --> 09:51.030
These kinds of unused planks... I'm sure 
every house must have stuff like this!

09:51.370 --> 09:53.960
I think we'll be able to gather a lot!

09:53.960 --> 09:55.280
Okay!

09:55.590 --> 10:01.000
Starting tomorrow, we're gathering 
materials for the secret hideout!

10:02.170 --> 10:03.420
Purin!

10:03.420 --> 10:06.370
Thank you for worrying about me!

10:09.490 --> 10:10.510
Sure.

10:15.760 --> 10:17.750
Stop that!

10:25.950 --> 10:28.350
Well, I guess it's okay.

10:37.100 --> 10:39.460
Stop right there, Serufu!

10:41.530 --> 10:43.610
Don't just leave ahead of me!

10:44.740 --> 10:47.400
Jobko-chan! Good morning!

10:47.400 --> 10:49.510
You're going to school this early?

10:49.510 --> 10:50.610
You, too!

10:50.610 --> 10:52.490
Oh! You're right!

10:56.170 --> 10:57.770
Serufu! In front of you!

10:57.770 --> 10:59.430
Huh? In front of me?

11:08.520 --> 11:11.030
Ow...

11:11.610 --> 11:12.180
Huh?

11:13.050 --> 11:14.140
That seems good.

11:14.140 --> 11:15.220
Yeah.

11:15.220 --> 11:15.950
Oh!

11:15.950 --> 11:18.240
Serufu-san! Jobko-san!

11:18.510 --> 11:20.160
Good meowning!

11:21.720 --> 11:24.160
Looks like you were thinking 
the same thing as us, huh?

11:26.910 --> 11:27.870
<b>Tree House</b>

11:26.910 --> 11:27.870
<b>Looking for Lumber</b>

11:26.910 --> 11:27.870
<b>What we're looking for</b>

11:26.910 --> 11:27.870
<b>Planks or other lumber you have around the house.</b>

11:26.910 --> 11:27.870
<b>Unusable desks and chairs, etc.</b>

11:26.910 --> 11:27.870
<b>Spare nails, screws, rope, etc.</b>

11:26.910 --> 11:27.870
<b>Anything and everything is OK! Please feel free to contact us about it!</b>

