11:27.870 --> 11:28.830
<b>Unusable desks and chairs, etc.</b>

11:27.870 --> 11:28.830
<b>Spare nails, screws, rope, etc.</b>

11:27.870 --> 11:28.830
<b>Anything and everything is OK! Please feel free to contact us about it!</b>

11:27.870 --> 11:28.830
<b>The DIY Club</b>

11:28.910 --> 11:31.250
<b>Tree House</b>

11:28.910 --> 11:31.250
<b>Looking for Lumber</b>

11:28.910 --> 11:31.250
<b>What we're looking for</b>

11:28.910 --> 11:31.250
<b>Planks or other lumber you have around the house.</b>

11:28.910 --> 11:31.250
<b>Unusable desks and chairs, etc.</b>

11:28.910 --> 11:31.250
<b>Spare nails, screws, rope, etc.</b>

11:28.910 --> 11:31.250
<b>Anything and everything is OK! Please feel free to contact us about it!</b>

11:28.910 --> 11:31.250
<b>The DIY Club</b>

11:28.910 --> 11:31.250
<b>Tree House</b>

11:28.910 --> 11:31.250
<b>Looking for Lumber</b>

11:31.240 --> 11:33.100
They're done!

11:33.940 --> 11:37.140
Let's make copies of these 
and post them around.

11:37.140 --> 11:38.920
Why are they hand-drawn?

11:38.920 --> 11:44.810
In <i>Sunflower Girls</i>, they made hand-drawn 
flyers to collect fertilizer,

11:44.810 --> 11:46.580
so I thought we could follow their example.

11:47.720 --> 11:50.530
They did collect a lot of 
fertilizer from that.

11:50.530 --> 11:51.400
Yes!

11:51.400 --> 11:53.310
So much that it caused 
problems for the neighbors!

11:55.060 --> 11:58.590
Then I'll get on the net and 
say we're looking for stuff.

11:58.590 --> 12:01.450
Last time, we got pallets 
from shipping companies,

12:01.450 --> 12:07.220
and Waku Wan gave us leftover lumber, 
so we didn't need to do it.

12:07.690 --> 12:08.700
Send!

12:08.980 --> 12:10.010
Okay.

12:10.430 --> 12:12.870
Our materials may have disappeared,

12:12.870 --> 12:14.550
but now that they're gone...

12:14.550 --> 12:16.550
We just have to gather them again!

12:14.550 --> 12:16.550
Let's gather them again!

12:16.550 --> 12:19.140
We've just gotta gather them again, meow!

12:16.550 --> 12:19.140
We've just gotta gather them again!

12:22.440 --> 12:24.070
Okay!

12:24.070 --> 12:25.460
Do it...

12:25.460 --> 12:27.800
yourself!

12:38.980 --> 12:41.980
Wow. A tree house.

12:41.980 --> 12:43.730
That sounds like fun, doesn't it?

12:41.990 --> 12:46.200
<b>Looking for Lumber</b>

12:41.990 --> 12:46.200
<b>What we're looking for</b>

12:41.990 --> 12:46.200
<b>Planks or other lumber you have around the house.</b>

12:41.990 --> 12:46.200
<b>Unusable desks and chairs, etc.</b>

12:41.990 --> 12:46.200
<b>Spare nails, screws, rope, etc.</b>

12:41.990 --> 12:46.200
<b>Anything and everything is OK! Please feel free to contact us about it!</b>

12:41.990 --> 12:46.200
<b>The DIY Club</b>

12:43.730 --> 12:45.730
I wonder if wood slats would be okay.

12:46.190 --> 12:49.020
I wonder if we have anything at home...

12:49.020 --> 12:52.630
They did some remodeling next door 
not long ago. Maybe I'll ask them.

12:55.210 --> 12:57.960
WAKUWAN Workshop

12:55.210 --> 12:57.960
Self-service

12:55.210 --> 12:57.960
Workspace

12:55.210 --> 12:57.960
Even without tools,
even without experience
feel free to Try DIY!

12:56.300 --> 12:57.960
Well...

12:57.960 --> 13:01.090
It says they're looking for 
any lumber you don't need.

13:01.090 --> 13:02.690
If you have some you can spare.

13:02.690 --> 13:07.470
It would be odd to say that it's in 
gratitude for these lovely accessories,

13:07.470 --> 13:10.970
but perhaps I'll bring in an old bookshelf.

13:10.970 --> 13:16.770
I'm not getting any younger, so it might be 
nice to clear out some rooms and tidy up.

13:16.770 --> 13:20.960
I'll contact our fellow senior citizens 
on social media and share this!

13:23.330 --> 13:24.920
Thank you so much!

13:26.400 --> 13:28.670
Ah, excuse me.

13:28.670 --> 13:33.450
We're from the Gata Gata 
Girls' High School's DIY Club.

13:34.090 --> 13:37.850
From the street, we could see 
that you have some planks

13:37.850 --> 13:40.960
leaning against something in your back yard.

13:40.960 --> 13:43.960
I-If by chance you don't need them...

13:44.260 --> 13:48.250
might it be possible for us to take them?

13:49.090 --> 13:51.600
Sanjo Spice Lab

13:49.090 --> 13:51.600
Today's Curry

13:49.090 --> 13:51.600
Uchimame Smashed Soybean
 and Dried Veggies

13:49.090 --> 13:51.600
Chili Chicken

13:49.090 --> 13:51.600
Rasam

13:58.610 --> 14:00.320
Stop.

14:00.320 --> 14:02.970
Zoom in on the right side.

14:04.990 --> 14:06.220
There, huh?

14:06.740 --> 14:09.160
Send a message to Shii.

14:09.160 --> 14:11.940
There's been a reply to 
our internet request.

14:11.940 --> 14:15.890
They said that they'd give us 
lumber if we'd come and get it.

14:20.820 --> 14:23.260
You don't mind letting us have all of this?!

14:23.260 --> 14:24.560
I don't mind.

14:24.560 --> 14:27.480
Those are all ones that broke 
during the typhoon anyway.

14:27.480 --> 14:29.380
This is such a big help to us!

14:29.380 --> 14:30.900
Up we go.

14:30.900 --> 14:32.230
Work hard now!

14:32.230 --> 14:34.110
And here, a little snack.

14:34.110 --> 14:36.210
Some sasadango I made this morning.

14:36.210 --> 14:40.260
Thank you! I gladly accept, meow!

14:56.170 --> 14:58.410
And so the grammar...

15:01.300 --> 15:03.230
Yua-san is one thing...

15:04.220 --> 15:06.570
but this is rare for Hikage-san.

15:09.930 --> 15:13.020
Let's gather and gather to 
gather as much as we can!

15:13.020 --> 15:14.300
Yeah!

15:13.020 --> 15:14.300
Yes!

15:13.020 --> 15:14.300
Okay!

15:13.020 --> 15:14.300
Meow!

15:14.680 --> 15:17.320
Please be careful not to hurt yourselves!

15:17.320 --> 15:19.050
We will!

15:19.290 --> 15:21.840
And let's be careful of 
jellyfish, too, all right?

15:21.840 --> 15:23.680
We will!

15:24.080 --> 15:26.190
Whoa!

15:28.820 --> 15:31.000
That stings!

15:31.280 --> 15:34.110
I gave you a proper warning, didn't I?

15:55.900 --> 15:57.520
Can you use this, too?

15:57.520 --> 15:59.750
Yes! That's perfect!

15:59.750 --> 16:02.240
The people in the house next 
door to me gave me these.

16:02.240 --> 16:03.720
Thank you!

16:03.720 --> 16:06.230
These are going to be used 
to build a tree house?

16:06.230 --> 16:09.260
That's right! They're going 
to become our secret hideout!

16:09.260 --> 16:12.250
Do it yourself, you know?

16:12.530 --> 16:14.330
Wow!

16:18.390 --> 16:21.000
We've gathered quite a bit, haven't we?

16:21.000 --> 16:21.860
Yes!

16:22.250 --> 16:30.840
Property of DIY Club
DO NOT Throw Away!

16:22.260 --> 16:23.470
But...

16:23.470 --> 16:26.330
Yeah. We need more.

16:26.330 --> 16:27.760
We need double this.

16:27.760 --> 16:28.890
Double?

16:28.890 --> 16:30.810
We'll work hard to get enough!

16:31.550 --> 16:36.470
Aren't there any homes being 
demolished or bowling alleys nearby?

16:36.470 --> 16:39.390
You already know there isn't a 
bowling alley nearby, right?

16:39.390 --> 16:43.010
Oh, yeah! That's right.

16:43.010 --> 16:45.020
Takumin, do you like bowling?

16:45.020 --> 16:47.580
N-No, I've never done it before.

16:47.580 --> 16:50.340
Let's go sometime! It's fun!

16:50.340 --> 16:53.280
Is it really necessary 
to talk about that now?

16:54.610 --> 16:55.720
Honestly...

16:55.720 --> 16:57.490
Jobko-chan, you'll go too, right?

16:57.490 --> 16:59.540
Well, yeah, I'm going!

17:06.420 --> 17:08.920
The next day

17:11.940 --> 17:15.410
Club

17:22.500 --> 17:24.620
Wow!

17:24.620 --> 17:26.980
Haruko-sensei, did you...

17:27.380 --> 17:30.940
I spent all night driving around 
a few hundred kilometers.

17:32.650 --> 17:35.180
I'll pick up the cost of 
the gas for you, too!

17:35.180 --> 17:40.630
And you're the one who told people not 
to spend their own money. Honestly.

17:41.100 --> 17:42.840
But good job!

17:42.840 --> 17:45.930
It's something I can do for you, as your advisor.

17:47.590 --> 17:49.190
Now that we have all of this...

17:50.360 --> 17:51.960
do we have enough?

17:52.120 --> 17:53.440
Yeah, we do.

17:53.440 --> 17:54.460
Yay!

17:54.460 --> 17:55.950
We did it, meow!

17:55.950 --> 18:00.550
Um... But how did you find so much?

18:01.000 --> 18:06.270
OGs. The "old girls." I tried 
reaching out to our alumni.

18:06.270 --> 18:07.510
OGs?

18:07.510 --> 18:09.980
Haru-neechan, you were in the DIY club?!

18:09.980 --> 18:11.640
Were you?

18:13.170 --> 18:14.890
Didn't I mention it?

18:15.410 --> 18:19.020
That's why I volunteered to be your advisor.

18:23.320 --> 18:24.850
Back then...

18:23.930 --> 18:26.400
DIY club

18:24.850 --> 18:27.730
we couldn't get into the club room...

18:27.730 --> 18:30.140
because there were so many members.

18:31.410 --> 18:37.430
Everyone had so much fun and enjoyed 
making things with their own hands.

18:38.680 --> 18:42.380
When we finished one thing, we'd move 
on to the next. And then the next.

18:42.380 --> 18:45.840
"What should we make next?" 
we'd ask. We'd get so excited.

18:50.990 --> 18:53.190
The ability to use cutting-edge technologies

18:53.190 --> 18:58.390
allowed for the production of highly 
efficient goods in great quantities.

18:58.390 --> 19:03.080
Once that happened, humanity was able 
to enjoy abundance inexpensively.

19:03.800 --> 19:06.570
Suddenly we're talking about 
civilization and culture.

19:07.310 --> 19:11.450
Moving forward, humanity will 
overcome many difficult problems...

19:11.450 --> 19:14.620
and the world will surely become 
even more convenient and abundant.

19:15.770 --> 19:18.780
However, using your own hands...

19:18.780 --> 19:23.120
Pooling your strengths with others' 
and making something together...

19:23.120 --> 19:24.600
That's a wonderful thing, isn't it?

19:25.570 --> 19:26.380
Yes, it is.

19:27.600 --> 19:29.190
Exactly!

19:29.190 --> 19:31.260
That's it exactly, meow!

19:31.550 --> 19:35.910
And DIY is really fun, right?

19:40.100 --> 19:41.040
Yes.

19:47.280 --> 19:48.890
This lumber...

19:49.330 --> 19:52.820
It's lumber that our club's 
alumni had at their houses.

19:52.820 --> 19:58.370
Even through the passing of time, 
they're still doing DIY like it's second nature.

20:00.380 --> 20:03.760
When I told everyone that you 
were building a secret hideout,

20:03.760 --> 20:06.320
they were overjoyed to provide materials.

20:06.860 --> 20:10.110
Oh, that's right. That club room we're using...

20:10.110 --> 20:13.060
was built by the first generation 
of DIY club members.

20:16.270 --> 20:17.420
Yasaku-san.

20:18.440 --> 20:19.600
Serufu-san.

20:20.820 --> 20:21.970
Hikage-san.

20:23.060 --> 20:24.320
Jobko-san.

20:25.580 --> 20:26.670
Kokoro-san.

20:28.660 --> 20:29.650
That is why...

20:30.990 --> 20:33.120
all of you will be able to do it, too.

20:33.120 --> 20:35.860
Carry on the heart and 
spirit of our alumni...

20:35.860 --> 20:39.290
and please do your best to 
build that secret hideout.

20:41.160 --> 20:42.260
We will!

20:45.920 --> 20:49.010
I wonder if they've gathered 
all the materials they need.

20:58.610 --> 21:01.790
This time, we're starting 
